# DTF tier manifest: ci-token-basic  (issue #2786)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single (the walking-skeleton topology; the auth
# asymmetry this tier gates is storage-independent).
#
# Feature (#2786): an OIDC / service-account API token may be presented as the
# HTTP **Basic** *password* (with ANY username) on FORMAT (package-manager)
# endpoints — /v2/* (OCI), /maven/*, /pypi/*, and the other registries — matching
# the `pip` netrc / Artifactory `token:<api_token>` convention used by clients
# that cannot send a Bearer header. The request is attributed to the TOKEN OWNER,
# not the (ignored) Basic username. The security ASYMMETRY is the point: the same
# Basic-with-token fallback is refused on the JSON management API `/api/v1/*`,
# which accepts an API token ONLY as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A token in
# the Basic password field on `/api/v1/*` must return 401 AUTH_ERROR.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (A) POSITIVE  — token-as-Basic-password (bogus username) PUTs+GETs a private
#       maven artifact -> 2xx, and the upload is DB-attributed to the token owner
#       (uploaded_by = owner uuid, NOT the Basic username). Pre-#2786 this 401s.
#   (B) CONTROL   — the SAME token as `Bearer` on /api/v1/auth/me -> 200 and
#       reports the owner. Proves the token itself is valid the canonical way.
#   (C) BOUNDARY  — the SAME token as the Basic *password* on /api/v1/* (auth/me
#       + a management route) -> 401 AUTH_ERROR, while a garbage Basic password
#       also 401s (sanity) and Bearer still 200s. This is the load-bearing
#       SECURITY assertion: the Basic-with-token fallback must NOT bleed into the
#       management API. Dropping it would make the tier a hollow pass.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives an admin login + a user create +
# user login + token mint + several format PUT/GETs and repeated /api/v1 probes
# back to back through one admin/user; the base default (ON) would throttle them.
# A tier that must disable a shipped control does so explicitly (design 2.2, same
# as the isolation / sso tiers).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
